  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The ancestral music of the Nama people of southern Namibia, inscribed by UNESCO on its List of Intangible Cultural Heritage in Need of Urgent Safeguarding. A leading melody and rhythm on the khab musical bow, the !guitsib guitar or the accordion is supported by harmony from other instruments, including the vlies (harmonica) usually played by women, with singing, humming and ululating, and it accompanies the Nama dance steps. The mouth-bow card stands in for the khab.",
